<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Built 2026-08-28: Francisco found "open a terminal and run a command every
  time" too much friction for something meant to be opened daily (logging a
  BJJ session, checking readiness). This keeps scripts/run_api.py running
  permanently in the background instead -- http://localhost:8000 is just
  always there, no command to remember or terminal window to keep open.

  Same per-user LaunchAgent pattern as com.healthos.morning.plist (not a
  LaunchDaemon: no root needed, only needs to run while Francisco is logged
  in -- a dashboard nobody can see while logged out isn't useful anyway).
  Binds to 127.0.0.1 only regardless (design principle 1), same as always.

  RunAtLoad + KeepAlive (unlike the morning job, which is RunAtLoad=false on
  a calendar schedule): this is a long-running service, not a once-a-day
  task -- it should start the moment the agent loads (login, or right after
  `launchctl load`) and restart itself if it ever crashes.

  Auto-reload enabled (2026-09-09 -- was --no-reload originally, on the
  assumption a silently-running service would never need uvicorn's
  file-watcher). Real, repeated finding proved that wrong: backend feature
  work happens directly against this same checked-out tree, not a separate
  dev instance, so a shipped Python change (new API route, new logic) sat
  invisible behind the still-running old process twice in practice -- the
  illness-log feature and the Trends-page averages feature both had to be
  manually restarted after the fact to actually take effect. scripts/
  run_api.py's reload is already scoped to reload_dirs=[src/health_os] (its
  default when --no-reload is omitted), so it only watches actual backend
  source, never data/health.db writes, frontend/, or log files -- routine
  sync/derived-metric writes don't trigger spurious restarts, only a real
  code change does. Trade-off, explicitly accepted for a single-user,
  low-request-volume local app: a brief in-flight-request interruption at
  the moment of an actual reload, and a small idle-watcher resource cost --
  both negligible here, unlike an actual production service.

  Serves whatever was last built to frontend/dist/ -- after any frontend
  code change, `cd frontend && npm run build` picks it up automatically on
  the next request (static files, no restart needed -- never did need one).
  Backend Python changes now also pick up automatically within a second or
  two of being saved, no restart needed either.

  Setup:
      cp launchd/com.healthos.api.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
      launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.healthos.api.plist

  Verify it's loaded and check on it:
      launchctl list | grep healthos.api
      curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" http://localhost:8000/api/today

  Manual restart is no longer routinely needed (see auto-reload note above)
  -- kept below only for the rare case reload itself needs kicking (e.g. a
  syntax error broke the reloader, or the plist/venv itself changed):
      launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.healthos.api

  Remove it (e.g. to free port 8000 for `npm run dev` + this script by hand):
      launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.healthos.api.plist
      rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.healthos.api.plist

  Output: data/logs/api_server_stdout.log / api_server_stderr.log.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.healthos.api</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin/uv</string>
        <string>run</string>
        <string>python</string>
        <string>scripts/run_api.py</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/franciscogostscagliarini/fitness man</string>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/franciscogostscagliarini/fitness man/data/logs/api_server_stdout.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/franciscogostscagliarini/fitness man/data/logs/api_server_stderr.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
